If you're not using the system Python, you should generally install it
using the Python you're using.


> I tried to install from a tarball but when I run the python program, I get
> the message that the packages were compiled in R-3.0.2 and it's using
> R-2.15.2.
>

That sounds like it could be finding the wrong R at installation time.
There might be an environment variable you can set to point it to your copy
of R, but I don't know off the top of my head.

Thomas

